note open/route.om: Open Humanity's shelf of open builds, inside forged. Prefix oh* (functions),
note go* (globals), to* (texts). Composed after the salvage and social slices, whose form reader,
note write precheck and session it uses (slformvalid, slgetform, slffeq, sowpre, soratev, soerr).
note A person signed in with a Radicle key names the Radicle id (RID) of a project that is not
note finished, or not right yet. forged does not fetch anything: it has no network and cannot run
note rad. It appends one line to <data>open/queue and the intake service (open/intake.om, its own
note program outside the sandbox) seeds and fetches the project within limits and rewrites
note <data>open/list.tsv, which this unit shows.
note   GET  <base>open/   the shelf: every project the intake accepted, marked unfinished and not
note                      verified, with its rad clone line; JSON when the request asks for it
note   GET  <base>open/<rid>   one listed project: its row and the snapshot the intake took (head,
note                      last commits, top-level files, README); JSON interplane/open-build/1
note   GET  <base>open.json and <base>open/<rid>.json   the same JSON under names of their own
note   POST <base>open/   action=bring (rid, note, consent=yes) or action=withdraw (rid)
note Queue lines:  B <tab> rid <tab> did <tab> note     and     W <tab> rid <tab> did
note list.tsv rows: rid, state, did, date, kilobytes, name, description, note. States "open" and
note "held" are listed for everyone; any other state is shown only to the key that brought the
note project.
note Every field is escaped on output. The queue is capped at 1 MiB (503 beyond it).
text topath "/open/"
text topat2 "/open"
